{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:PredictedSpectra.EmCouplingChernSimons","@type":"LeanModule","name":"PredictedSpectra.EmCouplingChernSimons","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.EmCouplingProjection","lean:module:QOU.Mass.QHookDimensionBalanced","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Determinant.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Notation"],"declarations":25,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.alphaEmInvGluonOctet_eq_partialSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.alphaEmInvGluonOctet_eq_partialSum","kind":"theorem","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/em-coupling-chern-simons.lean#L239-L248","doc":"The superseded form is the second partial sum of its own tower —\nthe concrete instance of `csTower_partialSum_two`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.alphaEmInvGluonOctet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.alphaEmInvGluonOctet","kind":"def","line":234,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/em-coupling-chern-simons.lean#L234-L237","doc":"The superseded gluon-octet form (second-order truncation). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.gluonOctetKappa","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.gluonOctetKappa","kind":"def","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/em-coupling-chern-simons.lean#L228-L232","doc":"The superseded coefficient `κ = 8q`.  The corpus's exact reading of the\n`8` is `Vol(𝓑₃)/G` (Borromean volume over Catalan's constant), not\n`dim su(3)`; either way the combination `q·8` was never derived and the\nlive `.md` uses the torus-knot Chern–Simons pairing instead. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.deltaCS_gluonOctet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.deltaCS_gluonOctet","kind":"def","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/em-coupling-chern-simons.lean#L224-L226","doc":"The superseded correction `ℏ_q⁴ · [5]_q` (balanced `[·]_q`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.alphaInv_eq_bare_mul_tower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.alphaInv_eq_bare_mul_tower","kind":"theorem","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/em-coupling-chern-simons.lean#L202-L214","doc":"**Conditional consequence (§3b-cond).**  *If* the conjecture holds,\nthe inverse coupling is the bare prefactor times the **full** correction\ntower `1 + Σ_{j≥1} δ_CS^j κ^{j−1}` — derived from the class's identity\nand convergence fields through `csTower_resums`, so the tower form and\nthe closed form are provably one statement, not two. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.ChernSimonsCorrectionConjecture.identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.ChernSimonsCorrectionConjecture.identity","kind":"theorem","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/em-coupling-chern-simons.lean#L200-L200","doc":"**The identity — the conjecture's claim.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.ChernSimonsCorrectionConjecture.tower_convergent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.ChernSimonsCorrectionConjecture.tower_convergent","kind":"theorem","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/em-coupling-chern-simons.lean#L198-L198","doc":"The tower converges: `|δ_CS · κ| < 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.ChernSimonsCorrectionConjecture.gram_nondegenerate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.ChernSimonsCorrectionConjecture.gram_nondegenerate","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/em-coupling-chern-simons.lean#L196-L196","doc":"The q-deformed pairing is non-degenerate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.ChernSimonsCorrectionConjecture.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.ChernSimonsCorrectionConjecture.mk","kind":"ctor","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/em-coupling-chern-simons.lean#L193-L193","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.ChernSimonsCorrectionConjecture","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.ChernSimonsCorrectionConjecture","kind":"class","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/em-coupling-chern-simons.lean#L166-L200","doc":"**Chern–Simons-correction conjecture** (primary, content-bearing,\nNO instance; `conj:em-coupling-chern-simons`).\n\nFor the substrate `q > 1`, a q-deformed Chern–Simons Gram pairing\n`Gq` and the inverse fine-structure constant `alphaInv`, the class\nasserts the `.md`'s identity with `κ` the Gram-determinant ratio:\n\n    alphaInv = q [9]_q [10]_q · (1 + δ_CS/(1 − δ_CS κ)),\n    κ = det G^cl_CS / det Gq,\n\ntogether with the non-degeneracy of `Gq` and the convergence of the\ntower (`|δ_CS κ| < 1`) that makes the resummed form the tower.\n\n**What is open.**  Which q-deformation of the classical pairing is\n`Gq` — the `.md` enumerates the 16 readings of *\"replace `m,n` by\n`[m]_q,[n]_q`\"*, the shipped producer picks one (`κ ≈ 1.7216`), and\nnone of the 16 makes the identity hold at the physical value (the\nresidual is `−468 ppb`; exact closure would need `κ ≈ 1.9153`).  So\n`Gq` is a parameter, and the class is falsified for every reading\nenumerated so far.  A parameter-free `Gq` is GAP bean territory.\n\nNo instance is provided; supplying one asserts the conjecture.\n(History: this class previously wrapped an `opaque` Prop, and before\nthat was discharged by an `axiom` installed as a global instance —\nboth removed, not completed.) ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:rem:em-coupling-chern-simons","label":"rem:em-coupling-chern-simons","md":"quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/em-coupling-chern-simons.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.csTower_partialSum_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.csTower_partialSum_two","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/em-coupling-chern-simons.lean#L157-L162","doc":"**The superseded form is the tower's second partial sum.** The order-`δ²`\nexpression `δ + κδ²` is exactly `Σ_{j=1}^{2} δ^j κ^{j-1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.csTower_resums","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.csTower_resums","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/em-coupling-chern-simons.lean#L144-L155","doc":"**The correction tower resums.** For `|δκ| < 1`,\n`Σ_{j≥1} δ^j κ^{j-1} = δ / (1 - δκ)`.  The closed form is not an\napproximation of the tower, it **is** the tower, so there is no\ntruncation order to choose — a chosen truncation order is a free\nparameter, and the superseded form had one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.alphaEmInvChernSimons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.alphaEmInvChernSimons","kind":"def","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/em-coupling-chern-simons.lean#L131-L135","doc":"**The conjectured inverse fine-structure constant** in the `.md`'s live\nform, with `κ` a parameter:\n`1/α_EM(q, κ) = q [9]_q [10]_q · (1 + δ_CS/(1 − δ_CS κ))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.csResummedFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.csResummedFactor","kind":"def","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/em-coupling-chern-simons.lean#L128-L129","doc":"The resummed correction factor `1 + δ/(1 − δκ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.deltaCS","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.deltaCS","kind":"def","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/em-coupling-chern-simons.lean#L123-L126","doc":"The Chern–Simons correction `δ_CS` of the `.md`:\n`(CS(T_{2,9}) + CS(T_{3,5})) · ([2]_q/2) · ℏ_q² / (q [9]_q [10]_q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.emBarePrefactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.emBarePrefactor","kind":"def","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/em-coupling-chern-simons.lean#L118-L121","doc":"The bare prefactor `q · [9]_q · [10]_q` — Layer 2 of\n`prop:em-coupling-projection` normalised by the force-carrier\n`q`-dimensions (Layer 3). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.hbarQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.hbarQ","kind":"def","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/em-coupling-chern-simons.lean#L115-L116","doc":"`ℏ_q = 1 − q⁻¹` (the mass-chain convention the `.md`'s `δ_CS` uses). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.gramDetRatio_congr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.gramDetRatio_congr","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/em-coupling-chern-simons.lean#L103-L113","doc":"`κ` is basis-independent: a congruence `G ↦ Bᵀ G B` multiplies both\ndeterminants by `(det B)²`, which cancels in the ratio (the `.md`'s\nfirst \"source of freedom\" is not one).  Stated for a common change of\nbasis `B` with `det B ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.gramDetRatio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.gramDetRatio","kind":"def","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/em-coupling-chern-simons.lean#L96-L101","doc":"The Gram-determinant ratio `κ = det G^cl_CS / det G^q_CS` against a\nq-deformed pairing `Gq`.  Which `Gq` — the reading of *\"replace `m, n`\nby `[m]_q, [n]_q`\"* — is the open identification, so `Gq` is a\nparameter here, not a definition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.csGramClassical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.csGramClassical","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/em-coupling-chern-simons.lean#L83-L94","doc":"**The classical Chern–Simons Gram pairing** of the `.md` for the\nconfiguration `(T_{2,9}, T_{3,5})` on Bring's surface:\n\n    G_CS = [ CS₁ + π² s₁²/c₁² ,  π² ℓ²/(c₁c₂) ;\n             π² ℓ²/(c₁c₂)    ,  CS₂ + π² s₂²/c₂² ]\n\nwith `s_i = (m_i−1)(n_i−1)`, `c_i = m_i n_i`, `ℓ = 17`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.carrierLinking_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.carrierLinking_eq","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/em-coupling-chern-simons.lean#L79-L81","doc":"`ℓ = |2·5 − 3·9| = 17` — the recorded integer is the formula's value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.carrierLinking","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.carrierLinking","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/em-coupling-chern-simons.lean#L75-L77","doc":"Linking number `ℓ = |m₁n₂ − m₂n₁|` of the carrier pair\n`(T_{2,9}, T_{3,5})`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.crossingProduct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.crossingProduct","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/em-coupling-chern-simons.lean#L72-L73","doc":"Crossing product `c = m·n` of `T_{m,n}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.selfLinking","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.selfLinking","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/em-coupling-chern-simons.lean#L68-L70","doc":"Self-linking `s = (m−1)(n−1)` of `T_{m,n}` (the `.md`'s Gram-matrix\ndiagonal datum). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.chernSimons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.chernSimons","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/em-coupling-chern-simons.lean#L63-L66","doc":"Chern–Simons invariant of the torus knot `T_{m,n}`:\n`CS(T_{m,n}) = π²(m²−1)(n²−1)/(12mn)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}